course: dictionary
lesson: 12880
title: Entail: what it needs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To entail something means to include it, or to need it as a necessary part. «The job entails a lot of travel.» So if you take the job, you must travel a lot, because the travel is part of the job.
explain: Ask yourself: what does this thing need or bring with it? «Being a captain entails being in charge of a team.» You cannot be a captain without being in charge. To check, swap in the word «involves» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Maths and logic use entail to mean «it follows that». «A number that is a multiple of 4 entails that it is even.» Context tells you which meaning is used: a job, a plan, or a rule.
fact: Entail is a formal word, so you will meet it in exams, reports and older books.
fact: Entail sounds like tail, but it does not mean an animal's tail.
fact: «Entail» means to include or need something as a necessary part or result.
fact: In logic, «A entails B» means that whenever A is true, B must also be true.
fact: In old English novels, «an entail» is a law that passes property down to certain heirs, often the eldest son.
exercise: «Looking after a puppy entails feeding it, walking it and cleaning up after it.» What does entails mean here? | Sells | Forgets | Hides from | *Needs or involves
exercise: «Her plan entails a long train ride and a short boat trip.» Which word could take the place of entails? | rejects | forgets | hides | *includes
exercise: «Being a twin entails having a sibling born at the same time.» What does being a twin entail? | Being very tall | Living in two houses | Speaking two languages | *Having a sibling born at the same time
test: «Running the school club entails setting out chairs and counting the money.» What does entails mean in this sentence? | Stops or ends | Pays for | Sings loudly | *Needs or includes
test: «If a shape is a square, then it entails that it has four sides.» In logic, what does entails mean? | It is not true | *It follows that it must also be true | Makes a sound | It is the same as a triangle
exam: «If a number is a multiple of 4, then it entails that it is also even.» What does entails mean in this sentence? | It is a kind of number | It hides the even number | *It follows that it must also be true | It is the opposite of even
